The FIGfonts in this directory are separate works from the program that reads
them. They are the twenty-four fonts TOIlet installs, copied unmodified from
its source tree, and they are redistributed here under their own licence.

Every one of them is by Sam Hocevar and is covered by the WTFPL. The
hand-written fonts state it in their own comment block, in these words:

    This font is free software. It comes without any warranty, to the extent
  permitted by applicable law. You can redistribute it and/or modify it under
  the terms of the Do What The Fuck You Want To Public License, Version 2,
  as published by Sam Hocevar. See http://sam.zoy.org/wtfpl/COPYING for more
  details.

    This font is part of TOIlet's official distribution. More information
  on the TOIlet website at http://caca.zoy.org/wiki/toilet

The remaining fonts — ascii9, ascii12, bigascii9, bigascii12, bigmono9,
bigmono12, mono9, mono12, smascii9, smascii12, smmono9, smmono12 — were
generated from libcaca's own bitmap fonts by the caca2tlf tool in TOIlet's
tools/ directory, and carry that tool's invocation as their comment instead of
a licence block. They are covered by TOIlet's COPYING, which is the WTFPL, and
by the grant TOIlet prints in its version banner:

  TOIlet, along with the various TOIlet fonts and documentation, may be
  freely copied and distributed.

Fonts from the figlet collection are deliberately not bundled: they are the
work of many different authors under many different licences, several of which
do not permit redistribution. Point -d at a directory of your own to use them.

